content:
dark-factory has NO /prd project overlay: `.claude/skills/prd/project.md` does not exist (only `.claude/skills/hotspot-survey/project.md` does), so the /prd skill runs in GENERIC mode on this repo. It therefore ELICITS path/manifest conventions per session instead of reading them from an overlay -- which is why the same conventions keep being independently re-derived and re-written to memory.

THE DE-FACTO CONVENTIONS to follow until an overlay exists (inferred from committed exemplars):
  - PRD files live at plans/<slug>-prd.md;
  - the capability manifest and its YAML sidecar follow the committed exemplars' shape -- and note commit_planning STRIPS hand-written comments from the sidecar, so durable explanation belongs in the .md twin, never the .yaml;
  - decompose runs under planning_mode with a bulk flip at commit_planning (wire dependencies BEFORE committing; a plain submit_task then add_dependency races the scheduler);
  - task metadata fields follow the manifest-table detail carried by the stamped peers.
WHAT AN OVERLAY WOULD BUY, per the newest peer: pre-answered G2/G3/G5 gate context, so the session stops re-eliciting it.
RELATED NORM, embedded in one peer rather than standalone: when a brief carries a load-bearing G6 premise question ("which physical model is true decides the fix"), resolve it IN the /prd session by direct verification rather than deferring it into the decomposed tasks.

ACCRETION: append here or add a stamped peer under topic `prd-generic-mode-overlay-absent` -- do not write a new unstamped entry. If an overlay is ever added, AMEND this entry: it is the record four separate sessions independently re-derived.
